ry 3.3 (Avatar Generation):** Avatar generation workflow provides the pattern for parallel image generation, storage, and metadata management that pet companions follow. [Source: docs/stories/story-3-3.md]\ndocs/stories/story-3-4.md:85:- Pet companions use the same art style system as avatars, enabling consistent visual themes when child's avatar and pet appear together in stories.\ndocs/stories/story-2-2-parent-login.md:32:- **Story 1.3 – tRPC API with Prisma ORM:** Provides the authenticated server context, TanStack Query client, and Prisma access used by `auth.*` procedures. [Source: docs/stories/story-1-3-trpc-prisma.md]  \ndocs/stories/story-2-2-parent-login.md:80:- docs/stories/story-1-3-trpc-prisma.md (context on existing API foundation)  \ndocs/brief.md:5:HeroKid is an AI-powered personalized storytelling app that transforms children aged 5-12 into the heroes of their own adventures alongside their real pets as magical companions. Using advanced AI (Google's Nano Banana), the platform creates customized stories where children upload photos to become cartoon protagonists in multiple art styles, with family members' voices narrating their personalized adventures. Unlike existing story generators that offer generic personalization, HeroKid creates deep emotional connections by featuring the child's actual appearance, their beloved pets as story companions, and familiar family voices as narrators, positioning itself as the \"Personalized Living Library\" that combines AI magic with educational substance.\ndocs/brief.md:27:**Core Concept:** HeroKid creates the world's most emotionally engaging personalized stories by combining three breakthrough innovations:\ndocs/brief.md:33:3. **Family Voice Cloning:** Parents' voices are cloned using ElevenLabs to narrate stories, creating intimate family bonding moments even when parents are unavailable\ndocs/brief.md:56:- Current Behavior: Prefer simple, linear stories with clear heroes/villains\ndocs/brief.md:62:- Current Behavior: Drawn to longer stories with episodic adventures and skill mastery\ndocs/brief.md:102:- **Story Completion Rate:** 85%+ of started stories finished by children\ndocs/brief.md:103:- **Return Usage:** Children request new stories 3+ times per week\ndocs/brief.md:105:- **Personalization Engagement:** 90% of children choose to include pets in stories when available\ndocs/brief.md:110:- **Stories Generated Per User:** Average 15+ stories per month per active user\ndocs/brief.md:126:- **Story Library:** Personal collection of generated stories with replay capability and progress tracking\ndocs/brief.md:140:- Children complete 80%+ of started stories and request new ones within 48 hours\ndocs/brief.md:159:- **Interconnected Story Universe:** Child's adventures build upon previous stories with recurring characters and evolving relationships\ndocs/brief.md:165:- **Physical Products:** Print-on-demand books of favorite personalized stories\ndocs/brief.md:219:- **Market Risk:** Parents may prefer traditional books/content over AI-generated stories despite personalization\ndocs/brief.md:259:- Children's focus groups show strong preference for seeing themselves and pets in stories\ndocs/brief.md:306:- Premium: Full AI generation with unlimited unique stories, advanced customization, custom plot requests\ndocs/brief.md:309:1. Hook users with quality template-based stories\ndocs/brief.md:311:3. Limit free usage (1-3 stories/week) to drive premium conversion\nweb-bundles/agents/architect.txt:1224:      2. Include all endpoints from epics/stories\nweb-bundles/agents/architect.txt:2533:      4. Include all endpoints from epics/stories\nweb-bundles/agents/architect.txt:3172:- [ ] Technical approaches for all epics and stories are addressed\ntests/load/stress-test.js:30:const storiesGenerated = new Counter('stories_generated');\ntests/load/stress-test.js:209:    storiesGenerated.add(1);\ndocs/PRD.md:85:- **85%+ story completion rate** - Children finish stories they start, indicating emotional investment\ndocs/PRD.md:86:- **Children request new stories 3+ times per week** - Organic return usage demonstrating genuine desire\ndocs/PRD.md:116:1. ✅ Children complete 80%+ of started stories and request new ones within 48 hours\ndocs/PRD.md:136:- **All Children:** 20 generic free stories always available in library\ndocs/PRD.md:137:- **Unlimited Re-reads:** Previous stories can be read unlimited times (no credits)\ndocs/PRD.md:149:  - Only for customized stories (child's avatar + pet)\ndocs/PRD.md:150:  - Generic stories always free\ndocs/PRD.md:161:- 5 stories + 2 avatars = 60 credits (~$6.00-$2.40 depending on package)\ndocs/PRD.md:168:- ✅ **Aligns incentives:** We want kids engaged (more stories) not capped by tier\ndocs/PRD.md:172:- Average family spends $5-15/month when engaged (1-3 stories + 1 avatar)\ndocs/PRD.md:207:   - **Cost (Generic Stories)**: FREE - 20+ generic stories always available in library\ndocs/PRD.md:212:   - Transaction history: View all credit purchases and usage (purchases, stories, avatars, pets)\ndocs/PRD.md:213:   - Free stories: 20+ generic stories always available (no credits)\ndocs/PRD.md:219:   - Personal collection: All generated stories saved to user profile\ndocs/PRD.md:222:   - Progress tracking: Bookmark reading position within longer stories\ndocs/PRD.md:238:   - Spending visibility: See which children are using credits and for what (stories, avatars, pets)\ndocs/PRD.md:241:   - Multi-layered filtering: AI content moderation on all generated stories\ndocs/PRD.md:281:   - Reading comprehension questions after stories\ndocs/PRD.md:292:   - Character development and growth across stories\ndocs/PRD.md:312:   - Print-on-demand books of favorite stories\ndocs/PRD.md:341:- Previously generated stories cached for offline reading\ndocs/PRD.md:379:- Story history: View all stories generated by child\ndocs/PRD.md:415:7. **Paywall appears**: \"Create unlimited stories - Choose your plan\"\ndocs/PRD.md:430:2. View current plan and usage (e.g., \"18 of 30 stories used this month\")\ndocs/PRD.md:475:- Pet type detection: Dog, cat, other (affects companion role in stories)\ndocs/PRD.md:512:- Parent reporting: Allow parents to flag stories as inappropriate\ndocs/PRD.md:518:- Favorites: Allow child to mark favorite stories\ndocs/PRD.md:519:- Re-read tracking: Count re-reads (popular stories for analytics)\ndocs/PRD.md:528:- Free allowances: First child avatar + pet free; 20 generic stories always free\ndocs/PRD.md:540:- Re-reads never cost credits; generic stories always free\ndocs/PRD.md:558:- Display all stories generated by child profile\ndocs/PRD.md:578:- Auto-cache last 10 stories per child for offline viewing\ndocs/PRD.md:579:- Manual download: Allow parent to select stories to save offline\ndocs/PRD.md:580:- Sync: Re-sync stories when connection available\ndocs/PRD.md:588:- View all stories generated by each child\ndocs/PRD.md:738:- PR campaign: \"AI bedtime stories that comply with new COPPA rules\"\ndocs/PRD.md:756:- Optimize trial length (2 vs 3 free stories)\ndocs/PRD.md:779:- Localization: Spanish language stories (large US Hispanic market)\ndocs/PRD.md:796:  - Shorten trial (1-2 stories) to create urgency\ndocs/PRD.md:801:- **Impact**: Paid users consuming 50-100 stories/month, costs exceed revenue\ndocs/PRD.md:828:  - Build brand loyalty early (emotional connection to \"their\" stories)\ndocs/PRD.md:865:   - Define database schema for users, child profiles, credit packs/transactions, stories (keep legacy subscription tables documented as deprecated)\ndocs/PRD.md:900:**Then**: `/bmad:bmm:workflows:create-epics-and-stories`\ndocs/PRD.md:902:- Create bite-sized user stories for development\ndocs/PRD.md:903:- Organize stories in priority order for MVP\ndocs/PERFORMANCE_OPTIMIZATIONS.md:48:@@index([childProfileId, createdAt]) // Child's recent stories\ndocs/PERFORMANCE_OPTIMIZATIONS.md:49:@@index([parentId, createdAt])       // Parent's all stories\ndocs/PERFORMANCE_OPTIMIZAT