is brownfield epic. Key considerations:\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:266:- If the scope grows beyond 3 stories, consider the full brownfield PRD process\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:292:- The enhancement requires 2-3 coordinated stories\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:298:- The enhancement requires multiple coordinated stories\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:433:- Draft specific, actionable proposed updates to any affected project artifacts (e.g., epics, user stories, PRD sections, architecture document sections) based on the analysis.\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:464:  - Identify the specific project artifacts that require updates (e.g., specific epics, user stories, PRD sections, architecture document components, diagrams).\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:467:    - Adding, removing, reordering, or splitting user stories within epics.\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1189:      This PRD is for SIGNIFICANT enhancements to existing projects that require comprehensive planning and multiple stories. Before proceeding:\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1191:      1. **Assess Enhancement Complexity**: If this is a simple feature addition or bug fix that could be completed in 1-2 focused development sessions, STOP and recommend: \"For simpler changes, consider using the brownfield-create-epic or brownfield-create-story task with the Product Owner instead. This full PRD process is designed for substantial enhancements that require architectural planning and multiple coordinated stories.\"\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1419:      - Size stories for AI agent execution in existing codebase context\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1586:      - Epic 1 must establish foundational project infrastructure (app setup, Git, CI/CD, core services) unless we are adding new functionality to an existing app, while also delivering an initial piece of functionality, even as simple as a health-check route or display of a simple canary page - remember this when we produce the stories for the first epic!\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1590:      - Cross Cutting Concerns should flow through epics and stories and not be final stories. For example, adding a logging framework as a last story of an epic, or at the end of a project as a final epic or story would be terrible as we would not have logging from the beginning.\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1602:      After the epic list is approved, present each epic with all its stories and acceptance criteria as a complete review unit.\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1604:      For each epic provide expanded goal (2-3 sentences describing the objective and value all the stories will achieve).\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1609:      - Each story should be a \"vertical slice\" delivering complete functionality aside from early enabler stories for project foundation\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1611:      - Identify and note any direct prerequisite stories\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1613:      - Ensure each story delivers clear user or business value, try to avoid enablers and build them into stories that deliver value.\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1614:      - Size stories for AI agent execution: Each story must be completable by a single AI agent in one focused session without context overflow\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1615:      - Think \"junior developer working for 2-4 hours\" - stories must be small, focused, and self-contained\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1641:              - Avoid cross-cutting concerns that should be in other stories or PRD sections\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1681:- Current project state (completed stories, current epic)\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1703:- [ ] **Identify Triggering Story:** Clearly identify the story (or stories) that revealed the issue.\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1730:  - [ ] Does the issue require changes to planned stories in future epics?\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1776:  - [ ] Can the issue be addressed by modifying/adding future stories within the existing plan?\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1780:  - [ ] Would reverting completed stories significantly simplify addressing the issue?\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1781:  - [ ] Identify specific stories/commits to consider for rollback.\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1812:- [ ] **High-Level Action Plan:** Next steps for stories/updates.\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:1859:4. Any existing epic definitions or user stories\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:2012:- [ ] Local testability requirements (e.g., via CLI) defined in ACs for relevant backend/data stories\nweb-bundles/agents/pm.txt:2111:- [ ] Schema changes planned iteratively, tied to stories requiring them\ndocs/stories/story-5-7.md:7:I want **to share and export my child's personalized stories as PDFs or images through private messaging channels**,\ndocs/stories/story-5-7.md:8:So that **I can share stories with extended family while maintaining COPPA compliance through watermarked content and no social media integration**.\ndocs/stories/story-5-7.md:29:- Supabase Storage bucket `story-pdfs` configured with 7-day lifecycle policy to auto-delete expired export files, reducing storage costs.\ndocs/stories/story-5-7.md:40:- **Rate Limiting Tests**: Generate 10 PDFs for same story within 24 hours successfully, verify 11th attempt fails with `TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` error, confirm counter resets after 24 hours, test rate limit is per-story (can export 10 different stories).\ndocs/stories/story-5-7.md:53:  - Fetch story from Supabase: `SELECT * FROM stories WHERE id = storyId` with `story_images` join\ndocs/stories/story-5-7.md:55:  - Upload to Supabase Storage: `supabase.storage.from('story-pdfs').upload(exportId + '.pdf', pdfBuffer)`\ndocs/stories/story-5-7.md:79:  - Settings screen toggle: \"Allow story sharing\" with description \"Share stories with family and friends\"\ndocs/stories/story-5-7.md:85:  - Bucket: `story-pdfs` with public read access (signed URLs only)\ndocs/stories/story-5-7.md:99:  - Monitor storage usage: Alert if `story-pdfs` bucket exceeds 10GB (lifecycle policy may need adjustment)\ndocs/stories/st